<title>UK: LPC-Ghana's Cocobod signs $275 mln loan.</title>
<headline>LPC-Ghana's Cocobod signs $275 mln loan.</headline>
<text>
<p>LONDON, Sept 17 (LPC) - Ghana Cocoa Board (Cocobod) signed in London today a $275 million trade finance facility, arrangers Rabobank International and Sumitomo Bank announced.</p>
<p>The 11-month credit was increased from $225 million after $440 million was raised in general syndication, bankers said. The loan is priced at 50 bps over LIBOR with a commitment fee of 20 bps. Borrowings are secured by fixed price cocoa contracts and receivables.</p>
<p>An international group of 43 banks joined the credit, including co arrangers Citibank and NatWest Markets.</p>
<p>--LPC Newsroom 44-0171-542-4048</p>
</text>
